# Scorched Geyser: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls an Island (one
# basic) and a Volcanic Island (the Island and Mountain types, but not basic, CR 205.4c): one basic is below the two, so
# its Scorched Geyser enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with an Island and
# a Mountain of its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Volcanic Island
Scorched Geyser
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mountain
Scorched Geyser
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Volcanic Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Scorched Geyser.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Scorched Geyser.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Scorched Geyser.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Scorched Geyser.Tapped = false
